    <dashboard _.fcp.AccessibleZoneTabOrder.true...enable-sort-zone-taborder='true' name='Summary'>
      <style />
      <size maxheight='800' maxwidth='1000' minheight='800' minwidth='1000' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='4' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone h='89375' id='7' param='horz' type-v2='layout-flow' w='98400' x='800' y='9625'>
            <zone h='89375' id='5' type-v2='layout-basic' w='98400' x='800' y='9625'>
              <zone h='47125' id='3' name='Heat map (Regions): Full-vax SPECTRUM' w='46700' x='800' y='51875'>
                <zone-style>
                  <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                  <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                  <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                  <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                </zone-style>
              </zone>
              <zone forceUpdate='true' h='35500' id='10' type-v2='text' w='40800' x='800' y='9625'>
                <formatted-text>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='8'>Goal:</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='8'>This dashboard aims to provide an interactive, data-driven tool for exploring vaccination rates across cities in Massachusetts. It enables users to analyze how demographics, age groups, wealth disparities, and grassroots organizational efforts affect vaccination outcomes.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='8'>6 Main Cities of Interest:</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='8'>The cities Wellesley, Framingham, Swampscott, Lynn, Chelsea, and Belmont were selected to explore how income differences and geographic proximity impact communities in Massachusetts. Wellesley and Belmont are wealthy areas with more resources and established networks, meaning they don’t rely as much on grassroots organizations. On the other hand, Chelsea is a low-income, immigrant-rich city where organizations like La Colaborativa are essential in supporting the community. These differences show how income levels affect access to resources and community support. By studying these cities, the project explores how factors like wealth, demographics, and local efforts shape vaccination rates and public health.</run>
                </formatted-text>
                <zone-style>
                  <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                  <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                  <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                  <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                </zone-style>
              </zone>
              <zone fixed-size='160' h='15000' id='6' is-fixed='true' param='vert' type-v2='layout-flow' w='14401' x='47500' y='84000'>
                <zone h='8125' id='8' name='Heat map (Regions): Full-vax SPECTRUM' pane-specification-id='4' param='[federated.04tfkjg1pvc6u213g4e920zibjms (copy 4)].[avg:Calculation_266767913857302528:qk]' type-v2='color' w='14401' x='47500' y='84000'>
